9,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.020830034120067585,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":29.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.015785708565053236,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":30.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.04319326360429792,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":28.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03325,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":22.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Rigel Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a biotechnology company, develops and provides therapies that enhance the lives of patients with hematologic disorders and cancer in the United States. The company offers TAVALISSE, an oral spleen tyrosine kinase inhibitor for the treatment of adult patients with chronic immune thrombocytopenia; REZLIDHIA, a non-intensive monotherapy to treat adult patients with relapsed or refractory (R/R) acute myeloid leukemia (AML) with a susceptible isocitrate dehydrogenase-1 (IDH1) mutation as detected by an FDA-approved test; and GAVRETO, a once daily, small molecule, oral, kinase inhibitor for the treatment of adult patients with metastatic rearranged during transfection (RET) fusion-positive non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), as well as to treat adult and pediatric patients twelve years of age and older with advanced or metastatic RET fusion-positive thyroid cancer. It also develops R289, an oral interleukin receptor-associated kinases 1 and 4 (IRAK1/4) inhibitor, which is being advanced to Phase 1b study for the treatment of hematology-oncology, autoimmune, and inflammatory diseases, as well as to treat lower-risk myelodysplastic syndrome. The company has strategic development collaboration with The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center (MDACC) for the development of olutasidenib in AML and other hematologic cancers with IDH1mutations; and the Collaborative Network for Neuro-Oncology Clinical Trial (CONNECT) to conduct a Phase 2 clinical trial to evaluate olutasidenib in combination with temozolomide in patients with high-grade glioma harboring an IDH1 mutation. Rigel Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Raul R. Rodriguez | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 172 people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 34%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $74K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Rigel Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $837M market cap on $294M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +35% over the past three years and +26% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at +56.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 4.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +56.7% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 43% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 38% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Rigel Pharmaceuticals' (NASDAQ:RIGL) Earnings Aren't As Good As They Appear","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-rigl/rigel-pharmaceuticals/news/rigel-pharmaceuticals-nasdaqrigl-earnings-arent-as-good-as-t","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488337.812,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.671,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rigel Pharmaceuticals (RIGL) & Its Competitors Head to Head Comparison